### Reading the failures:
###  * the first three are defect 1: with --quiet, --enable-testing installed the permission bypass and
###    printed NOTHING -- the consent notice went through say(), which --quiet suppresses.
###  * the next four are defect 2: --create-store-dir created BOTH candidate paths (the "not the other
###    candidate" and "not the <=27 path" lines fail in both directions), told the operator about only
###    one of them, and printed an undo for only one.

===== 2. the fixes =====
### defect 1 -- a printer that --quiet cannot silence (scripts/device/zl1-location-request.sh):
107-# under --quiet and the bypass got installed with nothing said. "Be quieter" means fewer read-only
108-# findings, never "do not tell me what I am about to give up"; the same rule the post-mortem harness
109-# exists to enforce on the other side (a mode that acts must be the one thing that still speaks).
110:warn() { printf '%s\n' "$*" >&2; }
111-hdr() { [ "$QUIET" = 1 ] || printf '\n== %s\n' "$*"; }
112-have() { command -v "$1" >/dev/null 2>&1; }
