===== 4. what this round does NOT establish =====
### * No device measurement, again: the fake /proc, the fake HAL process, the fake container and the
###   fake logcat are all synthetic. In particular "MISSING /data/system/users/0/fpdata" is the fake
###   root's answer, not the device's -- the real answer is still owed (docs 83's whole question).
### * The permission bypass is proven to be *announced* and to write exactly one file with exactly one
###   line; it is NOT proven to actually open gate 1 on the device. That still needs the device, and it
###   is the user's decision (docs 93 section 3.4 read the short circuit out of the installed library,
###   but a drop-in in the wrong directory is silently inert -- see the full-unit-name rule below).
### * The drop-in DIRECTORY name is the trap this harness pins only as text ("${UNIT}.d" survives the
###   rewrite): a bare lomiri-location-service.d/ is silently inert to systemd, which is the same
###   failure the update-machine-info unit had, and nothing on the host can prove otherwise.
### * --request's Qt client is stubbed, so what is asserted is that the harness's canned ZL1POS lines
###   pass through unaltered; whether a real client gets a session is the measurement the device owes.
